<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Expo '92</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1992</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Seville Expo '92</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Expo '92 was a world's fair held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, from 20 April to 12 October 1992, marking the 500th anniversary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>'s first voyage to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. Built on the island of La Cartuja, it received more than 40 million visits and brought major investment, including Spain's first high-speed railway, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a> and Seville.</p></div>
